  "XML03": "Late layer 17 MLP writes mostly in output directions favoring newline, end-of-turn and formatting tokens; confident prompts change little.",
  "XML04": "Layer 1 MLP is the main detokenization stage; tripling it is the most destructive early edit, flattening toward common tokens.",
  "XML05": "Late layer 18 behaves like layer 17: modest loss on confident prompts, larger shift of P4 and P7 toward generic continuations.",
  "XML06": "Layer 20 is a late MLP; amplification promotes high-frequency and formatting tokens with small effect on near-certain targets.",
  "XML07": "Layer 22 feeds the final norm almost directly, so its amplified output has the most direct logit effect among late layers.",
